I'm hungry.

806
00:31:14,227 --> 00:31:16,457
How are these eggplants so big?

807
00:31:18,467 --> 00:31:21,297
(She brings a big eggplant to the sink.)

808
00:31:22,037 --> 00:31:24,097
(Squeaky clean)

809
00:31:27,107 --> 00:31:29,237
(She cuts off the stem.)

810
00:31:30,677 --> 00:31:32,947
It doesn't go in because it's so big.

811
00:31:33,507 --> 00:31:34,747
I should put it on the top.

812
00:31:37,447 --> 00:31:40,816
(She places it on the bowl and moves it to the microwave.)

813
00:31:40,817 --> 00:31:42,416
- Will you microwave it? - Yes.

814
00:31:42,417 --> 00:31:43,417
(That's right.)

815
00:31:45,187 --> 00:31:47,926
People make a lot of eggplant dishes...

816
00:31:47,927 --> 00:31:50,497
these days.

817
00:31:50,727 --> 00:31:54,366
There was a recipe which cooked eggplants like eels.

818
00:31:54,367 --> 00:31:56,166
- I made rice with eggplant. - Rice with eggplant?

819
00:31:56,167 --> 00:31:57,366
Rice with eggplant is tasty.

820
00:31:57,367 --> 00:31:58,967
I'd be full after eating one eggplant.

821
00:32:00,067 --> 00:32:02,107
(Na Rae's rice with eggplant recipe will be revealed.)

822
00:32:02,755 --> 00:32:04,855
(Na Rae harvested a king-sized eggplant.)

823
00:32:05,125 --> 00:32:07,365
I microwaved it for three minutes.

824
00:32:07,925 --> 00:32:09,895
Then I cut it open and spread it wide.

825
00:32:10,795 --> 00:32:12,105
It looks delicious.

826
00:32:12,565 --> 00:32:13,605
It has been cooked well.

827
00:32:13,865 --> 00:32:14,905
All right.

828
00:32:15,735 --> 00:32:16,735
Oh, my.

829
00:32:16,775 --> 00:32:19,745
