1036
00:40:25,095 --> 00:40:27,924
- They were strangers, right? - Yes.

1037
00:40:27,925 --> 00:40:30,164
- Right? - The neighborhood is like that.

1038
00:40:30,165 --> 00:40:31,635
That's right. It's always like that.

1039
00:40:32,935 --> 00:40:35,305
(She walks down the street in a fancy outfit.)

1040
00:40:36,135 --> 00:40:37,135
(Impressed)

1041
00:40:37,535 --> 00:40:38,734
(My goodness)

1042
00:40:38,735 --> 00:40:39,805
It's packed.

1043
00:40:40,045 --> 00:40:41,274
Hello.

1044
00:40:41,275 --> 00:40:43,545
- Come on in. It has been a while. - It has been a while, right?

1045
00:40:43,845 --> 00:40:45,174
- Hello. - Hello.

1046
00:40:45,175 --> 00:40:47,214
Oh, my. I can't believe it.

1047
00:40:47,215 --> 00:40:49,284
- I can't believe you're here. - Sister.

1048
00:40:49,285 --> 00:40:51,384
- Sister. - Oh, my. Sister.

1049
00:40:51,385 --> 00:40:53,325
- Who is she? - My friends in the neighborhood.

1050
00:40:53,955 --> 00:40:55,355
- Your friends in the neighborhood? - Yes.

1051
00:40:56,325 --> 00:40:57,424
Have you been well?

1052
00:40:57,425 --> 00:40:58,495
(The owner checks in with her.)

1053
00:40:58,755 --> 00:41:02,735
This is the bar I frequent.

1054
00:41:03,335 --> 00:41:04,794
I visited for the first time after moving.

1055
00:41:04,795 --> 00:41:06,865
so I've been going for about three years.

1056
00:41:07,005 --> 00:41:10,275
Many Itaewon and Gyeongnidan-gil residents go there.

1057
00:41:11,475 --> 00:41:12,945
It's very atmospheric.

1058
00:41:13,745 --> 00:41:16,244
When you eat alone, you feel very miserable.

1059
00:41:16,245 --> 00:41:18,275
But when you drink alone,

1060
00:41:19,015 --> 00:41:20,814
it feels very atmospheric.

1061
00:41:20,815 --> 00:41:23,085
And here's the important part. In my neighborhood,

1062
00:41:23,915 --> 00:41:26,025
you never feel like you're drinking alone.

1063
00:41:26,355 --> 00:41:28,384
Even when you go alone, it doesn't feel that way.

1064
00:41:28,385 --> 00:41:29,554
They talk to you...

1065
00:41:29,555 --> 00:41:31,194
and ask you to drink with them.

1066
00:41:31,195 --> 00:41:32,864
I befriend people that way.

1067
00:41:32,865 --> 00:41:34,294
I love it so much...

1068
00:41:34,295 --> 00:41:35,765
that I visit quarterly.

1069
00:41:36,535 --> 00:41:37,665
What have you been drinking?

1070
00:41:38,165 --> 00:41:39,434
- Old fashioned? - What will you drink?

1071
00:41:39,435 --> 00:41:40,505
Hold on.

1072
00:41:40,965 --> 00:41:42,534
- Can you make a dirty martini? - Of course.

1073
00:41:42,535 --> 00:41:43,805
- Okay. - All right.

1074
00:41:43,905 --> 00:41:46,074
Is dirty martini the cocktail with crushed ice?

1075
00:41:46,075 --> 00:41:48,005
No, it contains olives.

1076
00:41:48,205 --> 00:41:49,514
It's a bit salty.

1077
00:41:49,515 --> 00:41:52,985
You have a conversation other people can join, right?

1078
00:41:53,115 --> 00:41:54,415
When I go to a place like that...

1079
00:41:54,715 --> 00:41:56,285
"How old are you? What do you do for a living?"

1080
00:41:56,555 --> 00:41:57,584
After we become close, I go,

1081
00:41:57,585 --> 00:41:59,015
"Hey, you shouldn't live that way."

1082
00:41:59,625 --> 00:42:00,984
- What are you talking about? - The moment you do that,

1083
00:42:00,985 --> 00:42:02,384
you'll get kicked out of the neighborhood.

1084
00:42:02,385 --> 00:42:04,094
What are you, a village teacher?

1085
00:42:04,095 --> 00:42:06,164
"You shouldn't be drinking, you punk."

1086
00:42:06,165 --> 00:42:07,924
It's natural to drink at a bar, you punk.

1087
00:42:07,925 --> 00:42:09,265
I end up doing that.

1088
00:42:09,395 --> 00:42:11,264
"You need to come to your senses."

1089
00:42:11,265 --> 00:42:12,705
Why do you even go to a bar?

1090
00:42:13,535 --> 00:42:15,775
When people stare, I go, "What are those punks looking at?"

1091
00:42:16,705 --> 00:42:18,204
"What are those punks looking at?" Come on.

1092
00:42:18,205 --> 00:42:19,374
- That's an old expression. - You're too old to be like that.

1093
00:42:19,375 --> 00:42:21,105
I have a different mindset.

1094
00:42:21,975 --> 00:42:23,914
You're so open-minded, Na Rae.

1095
00:42:23,915 --> 00:42:25,144
It's so hot.

1096
00:42:25,145 --> 00:42:26,185
(Glancing over)

1097
00:42:26,685 --> 00:42:28,715
Hello.

1098
00:42:29,255 --> 00:42:30,914
This place is great.

1099
00:42:30,915 --> 00:42:32,115
(She says hello to the customers across the table.)

1100
00:42:32,215 --> 00:42:34,525
- She's fluent in Korean. - Really?

1101
00:42:35,025 --> 00:42:37,494
- Her name is Da Som. - Hello.

1102
00:42:37,495 --> 00:42:38,994
- What? - She's Korean.

1103
00:42:38,995 --> 00:42:41,265
- Really? - She's a naturalized citizen.

1104
00:42:41,365 --> 00:42:42,764
Really? Are you a naturalized citizen?

1105
00:42:42,765 --> 00:42:44,695
Na Rae, don't you remember me?

1106
00:42:46,865 --> 00:42:48,634
We drank together last time.

1107
00:42:48,635 --> 00:42:51,004
- We had met. - That's right.

1108
00:42:51,005 --> 00:42:52,705
I went to Turkiye afterward.

1109
00:42:52,945 --> 00:42:54,675
I know. I watched all the episodes.

1110
00:42:55,005 --> 00:42:56,174
My goodness.

1111
00:42:56,175 --> 00:42:57,915
I was like, "That's my country."

1112
00:42:58,045 --> 00:42:59,544
Oh, my.

1113
00:42:59,545 --> 00:43:00,685
They're handsome, right?

1114
00:43:01,845 --> 00:43:05,055
You know, men in the Old Town were quite nice.

1115
00:43:05,285 --> 00:43:06,524
It was so nice.

1116
00:43:06,525 --> 00:43:09,424
She's Im Da Som.

1117
00:43:09,425 --> 00:43:11,024
- She's a naturalized citizen. - Im Da Som?

1118
00:43:11,025 --> 00:43:12,664
- Yes. - Im Da Som?

1119
00:43:12,665 --> 00:43:15,794
Yes. When she became naturalized, she took the last name of Im.

1120
00:43:15,795 --> 00:43:17,664
She's the first member of the Yongsan Im Clan.

1121
00:43:17,665 --> 00:43:18,794
She's the progenitor.

1122
00:43:18,795 --> 00:43:19,935
Really?

1123
00:43:20,505 --> 00:43:21,604
They were fine.

1124
00:43:21,605 --> 00:43:23,004
Here's your special martini.

1125
00:43:23,005 --> 00:43:24,675
Thank you.

1126
00:43:25,035 --> 00:43:26,945
- Cheers. - Cheers.

1127
00:43:27,305 --> 00:43:28,474
- Cheers. - Salute.

1128
00:43:28,475 --> 00:43:30,875
- Salute. - It's so hip.

1129
00:43:32,115 --> 00:43:34,444
(They do cheers and drink together.)

1130
00:43:34,445 --> 00:43:35,445
(My goodness)

1131
00:43:35,745 --> 00:43:38,784
This is the best. This is the taste I wanted.

1132
00:43:38,785 --> 00:43:41,585
You should come to my place...

1133
00:43:41,855 --> 00:43:43,755
and take some lettuce.

1134
00:43:44,255 --> 00:43:45,825
Do you grow lettuce at home?

1135
00:43:46,395 --> 00:43:50,135
I grow eggplants, lettuce, basil,

1136
00:43:50,395 --> 00:43:52,134
chives...

1137
00:43:52,135 --> 00:43:54,604
They must be hard to grow.

1138
00:43:54,605 --> 00:43:56,234
But the eggplants...

1139
00:43:56,235 --> 00:43:58,005
I only have one eggplant plant.

1140
00:43:58,305 --> 00:44:02,004
From a single plant, eight eggplants came out.

1141
00:44:02,005 --> 00:44:03,245
It's so weird.

1142
00:44:04,015 --> 00:44:05,114
Don't say that it's weird.

1143
00:44:05,115 --> 00:44:06,515
Did the plant bear fruits?

1144
00:44:06,685 --> 00:44:08,214
Yes, it did. I picked one.

1145
00:44:08,215 --> 00:44:09,385
You must be interested.

1146
00:44:09,555 --> 00:44:10,655
I gave her eggplants.

1147
00:44:12,485 --> 00:44:15,285
Hey, Turkiye. Let's have a drink.

1148
00:44:15,555 --> 00:44:17,454
- Let's have a drink. Okay. - I'd love that.

1149
00:44:17,455 --> 00:44:19,395
She's so fluent in Korean.

1150
00:44:19,465 --> 00:44:21,624
My goodness.

1151
00:44:21,625 --> 00:44:23,794
- Thank you. - You received it with both hands.

1152
00:44:23,795 --> 00:44:24,795
(Im Da Som knows the Korean etiquette.)

1153
00:44:25,035 --> 00:44:26,164
It's nice to meet you.

1154
00:44:26,165 --> 00:44:27,935
Salute.

1155
00:44:28,265 --> 00:44:30,434
(Although she came alone, she clinks glasses with others.)

1156
00:44:30,435 --> 00:44:33,874
- Everyone, be happy. - All right.

1157
00:44:33,875 --> 00:44:35,145
Na Rae looks so happy.

1158
00:44:35,305 --> 00:44:36,414
I'm so happy.

1159
00:44:36,415 --> 00:44:37,875
I love my neighborhood so much.

1160
00:44:41,415 --> 00:44:44,915
Today, I was a farmer at home.

1161
00:44:45,455 --> 00:44:46,755
Outside,

1162
00:44:47,655 --> 00:44:50,295
I was the empress.

1163
00:44:51,255 --> 00:44:52,325
For goodness' sake.

1164
00:44:52,555 --> 00:44:55,525
I like who I am.

1165
00:44:55,935 --> 00:44:58,835
I really like that I'm Park Na Rae.

1166
00:44:59,265 --> 00:45:00,965
I like everything.

1167
00:45:01,335 --> 00:45:04,475
This is the Itaewon freedom.

1168
00:45:05,005 --> 00:45:06,674
- It's hot. - It's hot.

1169
00:45:06,675 --> 00:45:09,145
My goodness. Stay healthy.

1170
00:45:09,345 --> 00:45:11,045
- Salute. - Salute.

1171
00:45:11,475 --> 00:45:13,914
- Health and happiness. - Health and happiness.

1172
00:45:13,915 --> 00:45:14,915
(I'm Happy That I'm Na Rae)

1173
00:45:14,916 --> 00:45:15,985
(I Live Alone)

1174
00:45:18,185 --> 00:45:19,885
Will this person be reincarnated?

1175
00:45:20,885 --> 00:45:22,154
(Sokcho Express Bus Terminal)

1176
00:45:22,155 --> 00:45:23,425
- It's Gangwon Province. - Sokcho.

1177
00:45:23,895 --> 00:45:24,994
Will this person go to Yangyang?

1178
00:45:24,995 --> 00:45:26,165
(Someone visits the Sokcho Express Bus Terminal.)

1179
00:45:27,525 --> 00:45:29,165
Gosh, what's up with this weather?

1180
00:45:31,435 --> 00:45:32,495
Gosh, he became so fit.

1181
00:45:32,765 --> 00:45:34,434
He has bulked up.

1182
00:45:34,435 --> 00:45:36,604
That's right. His chest became huge.

1183
00:45:36,605 --> 00:45:38,434
I gained 10kg.

1184
00:45:38,435 --> 00:45:39,444
(His chest is pumped up.)

1185
00:45:39,445 --> 00:45:41,704
- The shirt fits differently. - You look so cool.

1186
00:45:41,705 --> 00:45:43,775
That's right. You've changed completely.

1187
00:45:44,315 --> 00:45:46,584
- You definitely look healthy today. - Yes.

1188
00:45:46,585 --> 00:45:49,315
- The shirt fits differently. - I know.

1189
00:45:49,615 --> 00:45:51,715
- It's nice to hear the compliments. - I mean...

1190
00:45:51,785 --> 00:45:53,025
You look like Captain America.

1191
00:45:54,655 --> 00:45:57,525
(Captain Jae Hyeon came back with a new body.)

1192
00:45:58,595 --> 00:45:59,864
The sleeves fit snugly around his arms.

1193
00:45:59,865 --> 00:46:01,895
- I know. He looks cool. - Gosh.

1194
00:46:05,795 --> 00:46:08,135
- What's that? - A toy?

1195
00:46:08,265 --> 00:46:09,335
He'll like it, right?

1196
00:46:10,335 --> 00:46:11,834
There must be a baby.

1197
00:46:11,835 --> 00:46:13,045
(He walks with a toy box that's the size of his body.)

1198
00:46:15,945 --> 00:46:17,145
Hello.

1199
00:46:19,345 --> 00:46:20,784
Let's punch in the address.

1200
00:46:20,785 --> 00:46:21,785
(He takes a taxi from the bus terminal.)

1201
00:46:23,585 --> 00:46:24,955
It has been a while.

1202
00:46:25,685 --> 00:46:26,985
He'll love it.

1203
00:46:31,025 --> 00:46:32,325
I'm getting excited already.

1204
00:46:32,965 --> 00:46:34,625
I'm getting excited already.

1205
00:46:34,965 --> 00:46:36,335
I'm getting excited already.

1206
00:46:39,095 --> 00:46:40,705
(Gosh!)

1207
00:46:41,565 --> 00:46:42,705
That bridge.

1208
00:46:42,805 --> 00:46:44,035
It's perfect.

1209
00:46:45,735 --> 00:46:47,045
It's nice.

1210
00:46:47,605 --> 00:46:48,675
Goseong?

1211
00:46:49,945 --> 00:46:51,345
I'm excited.

1212
00:46:53,085 --> 00:46:56,985
(He heads over to Goseong, a place where an exciting encounter awaits.)

1213
00:46:58,985 --> 00:47:00,655
You aren't from Goseong.

1214
00:47:03,355 --> 00:47:07,564
(He finally arrives at a place.)

1215
00:47:07,565 --> 00:47:08,625
Gosh.

1216
00:47:11,035 --> 00:47:12,434
(Laughing)

1217
00:47:12,435 --> 00:47:13,505
Where is he?

1218
00:47:14,135 --> 00:47:15,304
Min Ji.

1219
00:47:15,305 --> 00:47:16,535
Min Ji?

1220
00:47:16,635 --> 00:47:17,874
- Min Ji? - Min Ji.

1221
00:47:17,875 --> 00:47:19,275
Is she a relative?

1222
00:47:20,345 --> 00:47:21,444
Min Ji.

1223
00:47:21,445 --> 00:47:22,744
(He continues to call for someone.)

1224
00:47:22,745 --> 00:47:23,815
Si On?

1225
00:47:27,745 --> 00:47:28,915
Hello.

1226
00:47:30,215 --> 00:47:31,355
Is he a nephew?

1227
00:47:31,955 --> 00:47:34,024
- It's a baby. - Si On, hello.

1228
00:47:34,025 --> 00:47:36,025
- What's that? - How cute!

1229
00:47:36,195 --> 00:47:37,224
What's that?

1230
00:47:37,225 --> 00:47:38,294
Oh, my.

1231
00:47:38,295 --> 00:47:39,995
- Hello. - Hey.

1232
00:47:40,095 --> 00:47:42,124
- Si On, hello. - You brought a really big one.

1233
00:47:42,125 --> 00:47:43,865
- What? - Hey, Min Ji.

1234
00:47:44,735 --> 00:47:45,934
He brought it.

1235
00:47:45,935 --> 00:47:47,405
What are you going to do?

1236
00:47:48,565 --> 00:47:51,105
This is where a couple I know lives.

1237
00:47:51,375 --> 00:47:55,175
Jeon Min Ji is a friend I've known for 16 years.

1238
00:47:55,445 --> 00:47:56,875
Then there are her husband...

1239
00:47:57,475 --> 00:47:58,574
and her baby,

1240
00:47:58,575 --> 00:47:59,784
- He's a baby. - Si On.

1241
00:47:59,785 --> 00:48:01,844
- Si On. - These three are together.

1242
00:48:01,845 --> 00:48:03,785
Si On looks just like his mother.

1243
00:48:03,855 --> 00:48:05,185
I knew Min Ji...

1244
00:48:05,485 --> 00:48:08,084
since I first started working as a model.

1245
00:48:08,085 --> 00:48:10,055
She was a friend of the manager I worked with.

1246
00:48:10,495 --> 00:48:13,695
She always helped at the back when I had shows.

1247
00:48:13,725 --> 00:48:15,194
What was fascinating was that she was the same age as me.

1248
00:48:15,195 --> 00:48:16,535
There weren't many that were my age.

1249
00:48:16,665 --> 00:48:18,835
- That was how we became friends. - Really?

1250
00:48:19,605 --> 00:48:21,034
It has been four years...

1251
00:48:21,035 --> 00:48:23,304
since I visited Min Ji's house.

1252
00:48:23,305 --> 00:48:26,304
I visited before Min Ji got pregnant.

1253
00:48:26,305 --> 00:48:28,544
She then got pregnant and raised her child...

1254
00:48:28,545 --> 00:48:30,044
- until a stable period. - Right.

1255
00:48:30,045 --> 00:48:31,715
We just talked to each other often on the phone.

1256
00:48:31,875 --> 00:48:34,614
Now that Si On has grown a lot, I decided to visit.

1257
00:48:34,615 --> 00:48:36,085
You've known her for a long time.

1258
00:48:36,415 --> 00:48:38,284
- I should wash my hands. - You can wash them here.

1259
00:48:38,285 --> 00:48:39,315
(It's his first visit after his friend gave birth.)

1260
00:48:40,755 --> 00:48:42,425
Si On is so adorable. My goodness.

1261
00:48:43,025 --> 00:48:44,095
Why is Si On so big now?

1262
00:48:45,055 --> 00:48:46,264
You should greet him, Si On.

1263
00:48:46,265 --> 00:48:48,295
Make a bow to your uncle.

1264
00:48:48,725 --> 00:48:49,965
You should make a bow to your uncle.

1265
00:48:50,765 --> 00:48:51,935
Make a bow.

1266
00:48:52,435 --> 00:48:54,765
- Gosh! - No. To your uncle.

1267
00:48:54,805 --> 00:48:56,304
He was the one who bought it for you.

1268
00:48:56,305 --> 00:48:58,134
- Hi, Si On! - "Thank you."

1269
00:48:58,135 --> 00:48:59,175
There you go.

1270
00:48:59,305 --> 00:49:00,305
Say, "Thank you."

1271
00:49:00,306 --> 00:49:02,274
- Give him a hug. - Give him a hug.

1272
00:49:02,275 --> 00:49:03,374
- Si On. - Give him a hug.

1273
00:49:03,375 --> 00:49:04,614
- A hug should be given... - Give a kiss on the cheek too.

1274
00:49:04,615 --> 00:49:05,845
as he brought the gift.

1275
00:49:05,945 --> 00:49:06,945
(Slowly approaching)

1276
00:49:06,946 --> 00:49:07,984
It's great to see you, Si On.

1277
00:49:07,985 --> 00:49:09,485
He's going to someone he has never seen before.

1278
00:49:10,055 --> 00:49:11,055
Give me a hug.

1279
00:49:11,615 --> 00:49:13,725
- "Thank you." - How adorable.

1280
00:49:14,525 --> 00:49:15,525
(Screaming)

1281
00:49:15,526 --> 00:49:16,594
- Give him a kiss on the cheek. - My goodness.

1282
00:49:16,595 --> 00:49:17,924
- The child isn't shy. - How do you give him a kiss?

1283
00:49:17,925 --> 00:49:19,194
- The other side. - Gosh!

1284
00:49:19,195 --> 00:49:20,225
- The other side too. - Here?

1285
00:49:20,425 --> 00:49:21,765
- Gosh! - Gosh!

1286
00:49:22,465 --> 00:49:24,695
- Gosh! - You're done now. Come here.

1287
00:49:24,965 --> 00:49:26,334
(What do I do?)

1288
00:49:26,335 --> 00:49:27,735
- You're done. - Si On is so adorable!

1289
00:49:28,065 --> 00:49:30,535
- So adorable! - The child is really meek.

1290
00:49:30,575 --> 00:49:31,834
That would make you want to buy more gifts.

1291
00:49:31,835 --> 00:49:33,075
Exactly.

1292
00:49:33,505 --> 00:49:35,274
Is Si On popular with the boys?

1293
00:49:35,275 --> 00:49:36,414
- I guess so. - Si On?

1294
00:49:36,415 --> 00:49:37,474
- Yes. - Si On is popular with the girls.

1295
00:49:37,475 --> 00:49:38,875
- Si On is a boy. - What?

1296
00:49:40,145 --> 00:49:41,184
He's our son.

1297
00:49:41,185 --> 00:49:42,745
- He's your son? - What?

1298
00:49:43,255 --> 00:49:45,114
- Wasn't Si On your daughter? - He's our son.

1299
