He's good.

2076
01:16:21,838 --> 01:16:23,808
- He's smart. - He is.

2077
01:16:24,738 --> 01:16:25,908
I'll wash my hands too.

2078
01:16:26,438 --> 01:16:28,078
Good. Let's go upstairs.

2079
01:16:28,538 --> 01:16:29,538
Let's go upstairs, Si On.

2080
01:16:29,539 --> 01:16:31,308
(Showing off good teamwork and friendship)

2081
01:16:32,578 --> 01:16:35,548
(Carefully heading to the rooftop)

2082
01:16:36,348 --> 01:16:37,848
Gosh, what is this?

2083
01:16:39,718 --> 01:16:40,887
(A wide open space)

2084
01:16:40,888 --> 01:16:42,257
- That place is nice. - It's nice.

2085
01:16:42,258 --> 01:16:44,687
I could see the ocean and the mountain from up there.

2086
01:16:44,688 --> 01:16:46,088
(A view of a friendly fishing village unfolds.)

2087
01:16:46,588 --> 01:16:48,057
- You should watch him. - Shall I give you a hand?

2088
01:16:48,058 --> 01:16:50,158
He shouldn't come near the fire.

2089
01:16:50,328 --> 01:16:51,927
Hang out here.

2090
01:16:51,928 --> 01:16:53,398
I'll make the squid dish quickly.

2091
01:16:54,698 --> 01:16:58,208
(While Si On is hanging out with Uncle Jae Hyeon,)

2092
01:17:01,308 --> 01:17:02,677
(Min Ji quickly cooks.)

2093
01:17:02,678 --> 01:17:04,578
That's the best kitchen.

2094
01:17:06,208 --> 01:17:10,548
(Adding lots of ingredients she packed in small portions)

2095
01:17:11,448 --> 01:17:13,318
Did you always cook?

2096
01:17:13,448 --> 01:17:15,887
Me? No, I started after giving birth.

2097
01:17:15,888 --> 01:17:16,957
- Really? - Yes.

2098
01:17:16,958 --> 01:17:18,587
- My husband used to. - Really?

2099
01:17:18,588 --> 01:17:20,158
- They wouldn't deliver in? - Never.

2100
01:17:20,258 --> 01:17:22,628
- There's no delivery either. - I bet there's no delivery.

2101
01:17:23,398 --> 01:17:24,997
We've never fed Si On outside food.

2102
01:17:24,998 --> 01:17:28,768
- Really? - I made all the baby food too.

2103
01:17:29,498 --> 01:17:32,508
Your mom is amazing, so is your dad.

2104
01:17:33,438 --> 01:17:35,438
(Putting it in)

2105
01:17:36,308 --> 01:17:37,777
- Gosh. - That looks good.

2106
01:17:37,778 --> 01:17:39,078
Stir-fried squid?

2107
01:17:39,148 --> 01:17:40,448
That looks good.

2108
01:17:42,718 --> 01:17:43,788
I'm done.

2109
01:17:44,548 --> 01:17:46,118
It's a really healthy meal.

2110
01:17:46,788 --> 01:17:48,458
Spicy stir-fried squid pork.

2111
01:17:49,658 --> 01:17:52,328
(Shall I show off my cooking skills now?)

2112
01:17:52,758 --> 01:17:54,928
I'll start cooking now, so can you watch the baby?

2113
01:17:56,458 --> 01:17:59,168
(Adding scallops to the boiling water)

2114
01:17:59,768 --> 01:18:02,298
(Boiling)

2115
01:18:04,838 --> 01:18:06,468
That must be good. Goodness.

2116
01:18:06,808 --> 01:18:07,938
It must be really good.

2117
01:18:08,908 --> 01:18:10,748
Uncle is making something.

2118
01:18:11,648 --> 01:18:13,577
He's making pho, which you like.

2119
01:18:13,578 --> 01:18:14,947
Pho?

2120
01:18:14,948 --> 01:18:16,348
Yes, pho.

2121
01:18:16,518 --> 01:18:19,117
As for the recipe, everything is the same,

2122
01:18:19,118 --> 01:18:20,687
but I'm using rice noodles instead.

2123
01:18:20,688 --> 01:18:22,458
Make broth first using scallops.

2124
01:18:23,188 --> 01:18:25,457
Boil rice noodles separately.

2125
01:18:25,458 --> 01:18:27,027
For the last step, turn off the stove,

2126
01:18:27,028 --> 01:18:29,027
and use the broth for emulsion.

2127
01:18:29,028 --> 01:18:30,458
He knows what he's doing.

2128
01:18:31,168 --> 01:18:33,628
(Pouring the scallop broth into the pot)

2129
01:18:34,868 --> 01:18:38,368
(Boiling the rice noodles first)

2130
01:18:40,068 --> 01:18:43,608
(Stir-frying the rest in oil while the noodles get cooked)

2131
01:18:44,248 --> 01:18:45,908
(Sizzling)

2132
01:18:46,048 --> 01:18:47,477
I used whole garlic...

2133
01:18:47,478 --> 01:18:49,747
because the baby can't have it. I wanted to take it out later.

2134
01:18:49,748 --> 01:18:50,788
I see.

2135
01:18:52,388 --> 01:18:54,787
(Hold on, Si On.)

2136
01:18:54,788 --> 01:18:57,158
(I'll let you taste a fantastic flavor.)

2137
01:18:58,458 --> 01:19:00,357
(Focused)

2138
01:19:00,358 --> 01:19:01,458
(Crying)

2139
01:19:01,828 --> 01:19:03,297
(He starts whining as he's hungry.)

2140
01:19:03,298 --> 01:19:04,568
You want to go up there?

2141
01:19:05,498 --> 01:19:06,527
(I'm hungry, Uncle Jae Hyeon.)

2142
01:19:06,528 --> 01:19:07,897
He's throwing a tantrum now as he's tired.

2143
01:19:07,898 --> 01:19:08,898
He's hungry.

2144
01:19:09,098 --> 01:19:10,367
Uncle will make it quickly.

2145
01:19:10,368 --> 01:19:11,767
Uncle is making delicious pho.

2146
01:19:11,768 --> 01:19:12,768
(Glancing)

2147
01:19:13,108 --> 01:19:14,138
Four more minutes.

2148
01:19:14,208 --> 01:19:15,508
- Uncle? - I got it.

2149
01:19:15,938 --> 01:19:17,478
He'd feel rushed.

2150
01:19:17,648 --> 01:19:18,648
I know.

2151
01:19:18,649 --> 01:19:20,008
(He quickly prepares scallops.)

2152
01:19:20,508 --> 01:19:23,077
(As soon as he's done prepping them,)

2153
01:19:23,078 --> 01:19:25,648
(he adds them to the pan with oil.)

2154
01:19:25,848 --> 01:19:27,618
(Si On is waiting.)

2155
01:19:27,758 --> 01:19:29,088
Cover it with the lid.

2156
01:19:29,558 --> 01:19:31,688
- He's waiting. - The baby is hungry.

2157
01:19:33,028 --> 01:19:36,658
(Move the cooked noodles to the pan.)

2158
01:19:37,058 --> 01:19:39,467
Si On likes perilla oil, right? We were going to use that.

2159
01:19:39,468 --> 01:19:40,567
The kid likes perilla oil?

2160
01:19:40,568 --> 01:19:42,298
He loves adding perilla oil to pho.

2161
01:19:42,498 --> 01:19:44,138
Really?

2162
01:19:44,468 --> 01:19:45,468
(Crying)

2163
01:19:45,708 --> 01:19:48,078
- Say, "Feed me now, Uncle." - Say, "Feed me now, Uncle."

2164
01:19:48,338 --> 01:19:49,677
- "Feed me now, Uncle." - "Feed me now, Uncle."

2165
01:19:49,678 --> 01:19:51,077
(Let's hurry.)

2166
01:19:51,078 --> 01:19:52,808
(Si On is waiting.)

2167
01:19:53,548 --> 01:19:56,077
(Let's go, Uncle Jae Hyeon.)

2168
01:19:56,078 --> 01:19:57,317
- How cute. - I'm done.

2169
01:19:57,318 --> 01:19:58,347
He's done.

2170
01:19:58,348 --> 01:20:00,688
It's ready.

2171
01:20:00,988 --> 01:20:03,858
- Gosh. - It's ready.

2172
01:20:04,158 --> 01:20:05,158
What is this?

2173
01:20:06,828 --> 01:20:07,997
What?

2174
01:20:07,998 --> 01:20:09,698
- What is it? - Kids can't lie.

2175
01:20:10,998 --> 01:20:12,227
Look at that.

2176
01:20:12,228 --> 01:20:13,368
It's all soggy.

2177
01:20:14,468 --> 01:20:16,268
- Gosh. - That's rice noodles.

2178
01:20:16,298 --> 01:20:17,837
- Rice noodles get soggy fast. - It looks like kalguksu...

2179
01:20:17,838 --> 01:20:19,608
stuck at the bottom of a pot after having shabu-shabu.

2180
01:20:20,238 --> 01:20:22,077
I used rice noodles because Si On likes them.

2181
01:20:22,078 --> 01:20:23,507
- That's why I gave it a try. - If you were to use them,

2182
01:20:23,508 --> 01:20:26,207
you should've soaked them in water for 30 minutes.

2183
01:20:26,208 --> 01:20:28,117
- That's right. - Then stir-fried it on strong heat.

2184
01:20:28,118 --> 01:20:29,417
That's how pad thai is made.

2185
01:20:29,418 --> 01:20:30,717
- Like pad thai. - That's how pad thai is made.

2186
01:20:30,718 --> 01:20:32,888
- If you boil them... - They get soggy if you boil them.

2187
01:20:34,318 --> 01:20:37,758
(Jae Hyeon's rice noodle pasta is super soggy.)

2188
01:20:37,928 --> 01:20:39,627
(With Min Ji's spicy stir-fried pork,)

2189
01:20:39,628 --> 01:20:42,098
(the table is filled with food made with love.)

2190
01:20:42,658 --> 01:20:44,868
(Thinking)

2191
01:20:45,098 --> 01:20:46,698
They don't look happy.

2192
01:20:47,538 --> 01:20:49,098
It looks like you'll have to add ramyeon seasoning.

2193
01:20:49,738 --> 01:20:50,938
Sounds good.

2194
01:20:51,268 --> 01:20:52,437
Let's eat.

2195
01:20:52,438 --> 01:20:54,378
What is this? Gosh, what's this?

2196
01:20:54,708 --> 01:20:56,477
- What's that? - Please cut them small.

2197
01:20:56,478 --> 01:20:58,107
(Please cut them small for Si On.)

2198
01:20:58,108 --> 01:20:59,747
I'll give it to you later secretly.

2199
01:20:59,748 --> 01:21:01,817
- Oh, no. It's all soggy. - It's soggy.

2200
01:21:01,818 --> 01:21:03,047
(Soggy)

2201
01:21:03,048 --> 01:21:04,988
You can't eat that. Oh, no.

2202
01:21:05,548 --> 01:21:06,588
Taste it a little bit.

2203
01:21:07,018 --> 01:21:08,757
- Open wide. - Wouldn't it be good for digestion?

2204
01:21:08,758 --> 01:21:09,787
How is it? Open wide.

2205
01:21:09,788 --> 01:21:10,958
(Taking a bite)

2206
01:21:11,058 --> 01:21:12,357
- How is it? - Is he spitting it out?

2207
01:21:12,358 --> 01:21:13,858
(Spitting it out)

2208
01:21:15,998 --> 01:21:17,098
- Really? - Oh, my gosh.

2209
01:21:17,298 --> 01:21:19,497
Kids spit out bad food right away.

2210
01:21:19,498 --> 01:21:21,167
- Kids are more honest. - That's right.

2211
01:21:21,168 --> 01:21:22,297
I was really surprised.

2212
01:21:22,298 --> 01:21:23,467
Adults lie...

2213
01:21:23,468 --> 01:21:24,808
- and swallow it, at least. - I know.

2214
01:21:25,808 --> 01:21:26,837
(Trying it again for the sake of Uncle Jae Hyeon)

2215
01:21:26,838 --> 01:21:27,908
- He's eating it. - He's eating it.

2216
01:21:28,238 --> 01:21:29,478
He's spitting it out.

2217
01:21:31,378 --> 01:21:34,048
Si On, I used rice noodles for you.

2218
01:21:34,578 --> 01:21:35,777
I hope it turns out delicious.

2219
01:21:35,778 --> 01:21:37,077
It's a shame.

2220
01:21:37,078 --> 01:21:38,818
Si On never spits out food.

2221
01:21:39,788 --> 01:21:42,958
Maybe the texture is new to him.

2222
01:21:43,818 --> 01:21:45,157
I won't try it next time.

2223
01:21:45,158 --> 01:21:46,488
(Sorry. I won't try cooking next time.)

2224
01:21:46,558 --> 01:21:47,957
Should I wrap it with dried laver? Open wide.

2225
01:21:47,958 --> 01:21:49,698
(Should I wrap it with dried laver?)

2226
01:21:50,658 --> 01:21:51,728
Are you spitting it out?

2227
01:21:53,398 --> 01:21:55,398
- Is it bad? - Try a bite, at least.

2228
01:21:56,268 --> 01:21:58,408
(Hold on...)

2229
01:21:58,738 --> 01:22:00,137
There's something inside, right?

2230
01:22:00,138 --> 01:22:01,477
(He found the noodles hidden inside the dried laver.)

2231
01:22:01,478 --> 01:22:02,837
I should've used pasta instead.

2232
01:22:02,838 --> 01:22:04,748
(Fine. Since Uncle made it...)

2233
01:22:05,008 --> 01:22:06,507
He ate it. He ate it even after seeing it.

2234
01:22:06,508 --> 01:22:07,918
He's rinsing his mouth with water.

2235
01:22:08,448 --> 01:22:10,418
He just wants to swallow it.

2236
01:22:11,248 --> 01:22:12,387
Like medicine.

2237
01:22:12,388 --> 01:22:13,787
- That's right. - That's what I did...

2238
01:22:13,788 --> 01:22:14,958
when I was told to eat kimchi when I was young.

2239
01:22:15,488 --> 01:22:17,788
He's eating it because you made it.

2240
01:22:18,488 --> 01:22:20,188
- Do you want to try more? - Do you want to try more?

2241
01:22:21,128 --> 01:22:22,928
(Unresponsive)

2242
01:22:23,298 --> 01:22:24,568
I mean, the noodles are too...

2243
01:22:26,398 --> 01:22:28,868
- Goodness. - Gosh.

2244
01:22:28,898 --> 01:22:30,167
- Maybe scallops... - Dad.

2245
01:22:30,168 --> 01:22:31,738
Maybe scallops don't suit his taste.

2246
01:22:32,038 --> 01:22:33,908
That could be the case. Because it's seafood...

2247
01:22:34,308 --> 01:22:35,908
Si On has never tried scallops.

2248
01:22:36,308 --> 01:22:38,278
(Feeling bad for some reason)

2249
01:22:39,048 --> 01:22:40,747
(The dad tries a bite instead of Si On.)

2250
01:22:40,748 --> 01:22:42,147
It's not bad.

2251
01:22:42,148 --> 01:22:43,318
- Is it? - Yes.

2252
01:22:43,818 --> 01:22:46,147
- I want this. - You want this?

2253
01:22:46,148 --> 01:22:47,148
It's delicious.

2254
01:22:47,149 --> 01:22:48,318
- Is it? - Yes.

2255
01:22:48,458 --> 01:22:50,488
But seriously, it must taste okay.

2256
01:22:50,858 --> 01:22:52,557
How was it for you?

2257
01:22:52,558 --> 01:22:54,298
It didn't suit my taste either.

2258
01:22:54,458 --> 01:22:55,458
They said it was good.

2259
01:22:55,459 --> 01:22:58,097
It's because I made it.

2260
01:22:58,098 --> 01:22:59,297
They're angels.

2261
01:22:59,298 --> 01:23:00,767
- He just swallowed it. - He almost...

2262
01:23:00,768 --> 01:23:02,497
pushed it into his throat.

2263
01:23:02,498 --> 01:23:04,137
I know. He pushed it down to his stomach.

2264
01:23:04,138 --> 01:23:06,007
Just like how you swallow a big pill.

2265
01:23:06,008 --> 01:23:08,078
He put the chopsticks down into this throat.

2266
01:23:08,638 --> 01:23:09,737
So it wouldn't touch his tongue.

2267
01:23:09,738 --> 01:23:11,577
- They're good-hearted. - They're really nice.

2268
01:23:11,578 --> 01:23:13,108
- "Good-hearted." - They're good-hearted.

2269
01:23:14,348 --> 01:23:16,418
- It's a shame. - Let's just use pasta next time.

2270
01:23:17,078 --> 01:23:18,347
- The drink tastes good, right? - Si On, I'll make something good...

2271
01:23:18,348 --> 01:23:19,788
- next time. - I'll finish this.

2272
01:23:20,588 --> 01:23:22,217
- Have the drink. - Your cooking's got a lot better.

2273
01:23:22,218 --> 01:23:23,887
- Here. - This too.

2274
01:23:23,888 --> 01:23:25,488
I couldn't even make rice.

2275
01:23:25,828 --> 01:23:27,757
It was my first time seeing you cook.

2276
01:23:27,758 --> 01:23:29,528
- Does this taste okay? - It's delicious.

2277
01:23:30,298 --> 01:23:32,598
(Si On has rice wrapped with dried laver.)

2278
01:23:33,198 --> 01:23:34,938
Is that really Mount Seorak?

2279
01:23:35,168 --> 01:23:36,368
- Over there. - It's that side.

2280
01:23:36,468 --> 01:23:37,508
That's the one?

2281
01:23:37,768 --> 01:23:39,038
- I want to go to Mount Seorak. - How nice.

2282
01:23:39,638 --> 01:23:41,177
How long has it been since you moved here?

2283
01:23:41,178 --> 01:23:43,038
Has it been six years for Min Ji?

2284
01:23:43,478 --> 01:23:44,507
It's been ten years for me.

2285
01:23:44,508 --> 01:23:45,908
It's been almost five years for me.

2286
01:23:45,948 --> 01:23:47,108
- Five years? - Yes.

2287
01:23:48,878 --> 01:23:51,687
If Si On grows a little more,

2288
01:23:51,688 --> 01:23:52,818
will you move to the city?

2289
01:23:53,048 --> 01:23:54,488
- No. - You won't?

2290
01:23:54,758 --> 01:23:55,817
As for elementary, middle, and high school...

2291
01:23:55,818 --> 01:23:56,888
I like it better here.

2292
01:23:57,388 --> 01:23:59,127
- As for elementary school, - For high school...

2293
01:23:59,128 --> 01:24:01,128
even kids from Seoul and Gyeonggi Province move here.

2294
01:24:01,428 --> 01:24:02,527
- Really? - To live here.

2295
01:24:02,528 --> 01:24:04,568
There are many after-school activities here.

2296
01:24:04,668 --> 01:24:06,097
- I see. - Kids move there instead.

2297
01:24:06,098 --> 01:24:07,468
- That's right. - That's understandable.

2298
01:24:07,768 --> 01:24:09,767
Kids living here learn surfing for free.

2299
01:24:09,768 --> 01:24:11,268
- Really? - I see.

2300
01:24:11,738 --> 01:24:12,968
Golf and horseback riding.

2301
01:24:13,338 --> 01:24:15,078
- They learn horseback riding too? - Golf and horseback riding too?

2302
01:24:15,278 --> 01:24:18,377
Kids move to the country instead of moving to Seoul.

2303
01:24:18,378 --> 01:24:20,377
So that they can have proper education.

2304
01:24:20,378 --> 01:24:22,047
Since there's golf and horseback riding.

2305
01:24:22,048 --> 01:24:23,977
- That's right. - The spectrum is wide.

2306
01:24:23,978 --> 01:24:25,018
(There are more diverse educational environment options now.)

2307
01:24:26,288 --> 01:24:27,918
I think you won't have any worries...

2308
01:24:28,358 --> 01:24:29,521
if you live here.

2309
01:24:29,758 --> 01:24:31,487
I like how it's not loud here.

2310
01:24:31,488 --> 01:24:34,698
When you're floating on the ocean,

2311
01:24:35,598 --> 01:24:37,768
you flow naturally. I liked that feeling.

2312
01:24:38,298 --> 01:24:39,397
- When you float... - He likes it.

2313
01:24:39,398 --> 01:24:40,468
I know.

2314
01:24:42,598 --> 01:24:43,838
You know, though,

2315
01:24:45,808 --> 01:24:47,437
this scenery feels really strange.

2316
01:24:47,438 --> 01:24:49,138
- It feels foreign. - Why?

2317
01:24:49,978 --> 01:24:53,578
It's really fascinating how Min Ji became a mom.

2318
01:24:53,708 --> 01:24:56,278
- To that extent? - Yes, it's really fascinating.

2319
01:24:56,648 --> 01:24:57,948
She's a fool for her son.

2320
01:24:59,148 --> 01:25:01,458
(Heave-ho!)

2321
01:25:02,188 --> 01:25:03,518
- He's full of energy. - I know.

2322
01:25:04,358 --> 01:25:07,188
There are many kinds of fortunes,

2323
01:25:07,388 --> 01:25:09,658
but I think I'm really fortunate with people.

2324
01:25:10,298 --> 01:25:12,968
I say that because the more time goes by,

2325
01:25:13,068 --> 01:25:14,868
I feel more proud of my friends.

2326
01:25:15,338 --> 01:25:16,837
They're doing so well...

2327
01:25:16,838 --> 01:25:18,908
in a healthy way.

2328
01:25:19,068 --> 01:25:20,937
- That itself makes me happy. - He's right.

2329
01:25:20,938 --> 01:25:22,908
You know how we say, "Jackpot" when we find ginseng?

2330
01:25:23,178 --> 01:25:25,607
I'm just the ground,

2331
01:25:25,608 --> 01:25:26,608
whereas my friends are ginseng.

2332
01:25:27,348 --> 01:25:30,217
There are so many people I say "Jackpot" to,

2333
01:25:30,218 --> 01:25:31,348
so I'm really happy.

2334
01:25:32,818 --> 01:25:34,087
It's when the sunset is the prettiest.

2335
01:25:34,088 --> 01:25:35,687
- Goodness. - Gosh, it's pretty.

2336
01:25:35,688 --> 01:25:37,218
Si On, look at the sky.

2337
01:25:37,758 --> 01:25:39,788
- Goodness. - It's pink.

2338
01:25:40,528 --> 01:25:42,957
There's another reason for me to come here.

2339
01:25:42,958 --> 01:25:43,958
Si On.

2340
01:25:44,368 --> 01:25:45,567
We had fun by ourselves...

2341
01:25:45,568 --> 01:25:47,168
- back then. - That's right.

2342
01:25:47,698 --> 01:25:49,237
But having an additional member,

2343
01:25:49,238 --> 01:25:50,438
it's a different kind of fun.

2344
01:25:51,108 --> 01:25:53,168
I feel like Si On will grow really fast,

2345
01:25:53,438 --> 01:25:54,678
so I should come often.

2346
01:25:55,178 --> 01:25:57,037
- He grows really fast. - Kids grow so fast.

2347
01:25:57,038 --> 01:25:59,648
(Blessed with Good Relationships, Overflowing Happiness)

2348
01:25:59,908 --> 01:26:01,518
(Next story)

2349
01:26:02,878 --> 01:26:05,248
(A fresh and lively summer full of vitality)

2350
01:26:07,858 --> 01:26:09,788
(Dae Ho's vivarium is filled with vitality as well.)

2351
01:26:11,788 --> 01:26:13,428
(How will his rooftop look?)

2352
01:26:15,898 --> 01:26:17,328
(Gosh, how did it turn out this way?)

2353
01:26:17,798 --> 01:26:19,267
It rained so much.

2354
01:26:19,268 --> 01:26:22,638
(There was too much vitality.)

2355
01:26:24,338 --> 01:26:26,637
(Excessive spurt of vitality)

2356
01:26:26,638 --> 01:26:28,407
It twines as it goes up.

2357
01:26:28,408 --> 01:26:29,637
So even if I get rid of them...

2358
01:26:29,638 --> 01:26:31,808
(What's even worse is Damarghini wrapped with vines.)

2359
01:26:32,208 --> 01:26:33,808
How did this grow on a car?

2360
01:26:34,678 --> 01:26:36,848
(It must be possessed by the vine evil spirit.)

2361
01:26:37,148 --> 01:26:38,148
Gosh, it's so hot.

2362
01:26:38,149 --> 01:26:41,088
(Go away, evil spirit.)

2363
01:26:43,018 --> 01:26:44,317
(Revving)

2364
01:26:44,318 --> 01:26:46,428
(Damarghini, let's fly again.)

2365
01:26:47,458 --> 01:26:48,898
(Celebrating the extermination of the evil spirit)

2366
01:26:49,898 --> 01:26:51,428
(He refreshingly washes it as well.)

2367
01:26:55,268 --> 01:26:56,468
(What is this?)

2368
01:26:57,368 --> 01:26:58,768
(Why is it giving out this kind of color?)

2369
01:27:00,038 --> 01:27:02,708
(Damarghini is shedding black tears.)

2370
01:27:04,848 --> 01:27:07,378
(The evil spirit returned without dying.)

2371
01:27:09,078 --> 01:27:12,648
(I Saw the Evil Damarghini)

2372
01:27:13,188 --> 01:27:14,188
(Turning)

2373
01:27:14,189 --> 01:27:15,588
(An inexplicable movement)

2374
01:27:16,488 --> 01:27:18,057
(Stepping on the brake)

2375
01:27:18,058 --> 01:27:19,088
Oh, no.

2376
01:27:22,098 --> 01:27:23,457
(I'm going to get a driver's license today.)

2377
01:27:23,458 --> 01:27:24,998
(As Dudu's guardian...)

2378
01:27:25,998 --> 01:27:29,498
(She has to take him to the hospital if he gets sick.)

2379
01:27:30,238 --> 01:27:32,538
(I must have a driver's license.)

2380
01:27:33,708 --> 01:27:34,807
(Filled with fascinating equipment)

2381
01:27:34,808 --> 01:27:36,538
(A simulator training center for driving skills)

2382
01:27:37,208 --> 01:27:38,578
(Turning)

2383
01:27:41,248 --> 01:27:42,918
(Disqualified)

2384
01:27:43,518 --> 01:27:45,588
(A parade of minus points)

2385
01:27:46,118 --> 01:27:47,718
(What do I do?)

2386
01:27:48,558 --> 01:27:50,918
(Lee Jung, you should pull yourself together.)

2387
01:27:51,528 --> 01:27:52,927
(Can I try one last time?)

2388
01:27:52,928 --> 01:27:53,928
That's good.

2389
01:27:53,929 --> 01:27:55,758
(Awakened)

2390
01:27:56,558 --> 01:27:58,698
(Yes, nothing is impossible!)

2391
01:27:59,428 --> 01:28:01,737
(Maybe...)

2392
01:28:01,738 --> 01:28:03,268
(I'm a genius.)

2393
01:28:05,338 --> 01:28:07,438
(A driver's license test? I'll easily pass.)

2394
01:28:08,278 --> 01:28:10,208
All the good energy is coming to me.

2395
01:28:10,408 --> 01:28:11,678
(A truck?)

2396
01:28:12,178 --> 01:28:14,107
(Yes, let's give it a try...)

2397
01:28:14,108 --> 01:28:15,578
(getting a Type 1 driver's license.)

2398
01:28:16,518 --> 01:28:18,047
(Since that's cool.)

2399
01:28:18,048 --> 01:28:19,048
Let's start.

2400
01:28:19,049 --> 01:28:22,888
(I Am a Genius Type One Driver)
